# .antigravityrules — leafylog Agent Roles

## [Coding Constraints — All Agents]

### State Management [ABSOLUTE]
- Use `flutter_riverpod` exclusively. `setState`, `ChangeNotifier`, `BLoC`, and non-Riverpod `Provider` are forbidden.
- All business logic must live in Providers. Page widgets must not contain business logic.
- Apply Optimistic Update in `StateNotifier` (update memory first, then sync to disk).
- `FutureProvider.family`: declare cache invalidation policy explicitly.
- Provider overrides only in `main.dart`'s `ProviderScope`.

### Hive Serialization [ABSOLUTE]
- All Hive model classes require `@HiveType` + `@HiveField` annotations; adapters generated via `build_runner`.
- Never change existing `typeId` or `fieldId` — doing so breaks stored data compatibility.
- New fields must be nullable or have a `defaultValue`.
- After any model change: `flutter pub run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs`.

### Data Access
- JSON files are the source of truth. Hive is cache/settings only.
- All file access must go through `FileSystemRepository`. No direct `dart:io` reads/writes.
- Plant ID: UUID v4. Check `plants.json` for duplicates before registering.
- Photo path: `[AppDocDir]/leafylog/plants/{FULL_UUID}/photos/YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_PlantID8자리.jpg`

### Architecture Boundaries
- `presentation/` must not depend directly on `data/`. Route through `providers/` or `domain/`.
- `domain/usecases/` UseCase classes: pure Dart, no Flutter framework dependency.

### Flutter Structure [CRITICAL]
- Do not move or rename files in `lib/`, `android/`, `ios/`, or `pubspec.yaml`.
- After `pubspec.yaml` dependency changes: instruct the user to run `flutter pub get`.
- Never edit generated files (`*.g.dart`) directly — always regenerate via `build_runner`.

